{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfj0lgtpk5","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"FeatureBench onboard learner needs ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 in spawn env or its Write is gate-blocked","summary":"scripts/onboard.js / onboard-learn.js spawn the agentic learner with a deliberately empty MCP config (bench/mcp-off.json, --strict-mcp-config) so it has NO orchestrator claim tools. But the spawned learner inherits the parent env, so the orch-gate PreToolUse hook is still active in that sub-session — and with no branch_task/start_task available, the learner cannot claim a task to satisfy the gate. Result: its final Write of onboard-notes.json is blocked (orch-gate: no task claimed), the agent dumps the kept/rejected JSON into its result text instead, and onboard.js reports the misleading 'learner did not produce onboard-notes.json (sandboxed?)'. FIX: export ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 before running onboard.js / onboard-learn.js — it propagates to the spawned learner (spawnSync inherits env) and ungates its Write. Confirmed on pandas @82fa2715: with the flag the learner wrote onboard-notes.json (kept 13 / rejected 13 of 500) in 148s. This is NOT a true sandbox failure; the 'sandboxed?' hint in onboard.js is wrong for this workspace.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T18:08:04.013Z","vec":[-0.08993847668170929,-0.010170551016926765,-0.019994031637907028,0.010737431235611439,0.053442128002643585,-0.024329349398612976,0.027022697031497955,0.004440581426024437,-0.01746591366827488,0.07091573625802994,0.004833701997995377,-0.034951891750097275,-0.02470632642507553,0.027699580416083336,0.0270865298807621,0.05633409693837166,0.07843068987131119,-0.09088823199272156,0.006247201468795538,-0.01890137791633606,0.008711104281246662,-0.03575960546731949,0.022060904651880264,0.02109653875231743,-0.03792266175150871,-0.03698815032839775,-0.03928184136748314,-0.027414925396442413,0.01133348885923624,-0.018499359488487244,-0.00491742230951786,0.11507119983434677,-0.025161851197481155,-0